ían 19,8 contratos. La razón entre observados y esperados es 3,4, con un intervalo de confianza del 95 % de 2,5 a 4,7. En diciembre se adjudicó el 10 % de los contratos junto al límite, mientras que diciembre supone el 12 % de todos sus contratos de servicios y suministros. Los contratos junto al límite se reparten entre 40 adjudicatarios distintos. El contrato [1], de 14.800 euros, se adjudicó en diciembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: La concentración de contratos al límite no implica irregularidades. Puede deberse a razones legítimas, como necesidades específicas o precios de mercado.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1] y [2] atienden la misma necesidad. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en otros sectores. Analizar si los contratos al límite se distribuyen uniformemente en el tiempo.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 68 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 19.8 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 3.4, with a 95% confidence interval of 2.5 to 4.7. December accounts for 10% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 12% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 10. Contract [1], for 14,800 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December and the high number of awardees do not indicate improper conduct. These could reflect normal market conditions or budget constraints, not wrongdoing.\nWhat can be checked: Check the contracts awarded in December for consistency with other contracts from the same awardee. Review the most frequent awardee to ensure no single supplier is overused. Look for patterns in contract values and dates to confirm if they align with standard procurement practices.","or